   "evidence": "The general expression expands to `l(l-1) x^(l-2) G l x - (2l+1) x^l G (l+1) x + x^(l+2) G (l+2) x`; substituting `x^2 * G (l+2) x = (2l+3) * G (l+1) x - G l x` (`sphericalBesselJDivPow_add_two`, line 242) gives `l(l-1) x^(l-2) G l x + 2 x^l G (l+1) x - x^l G l x`, which is `-(2/x) * deriv (sphericalBesselJ l) x + (l(l+1)/x^2 - 1) * sphericalBesselJ l x` expanded with `sphericalBesselJ_def` and `deriv_sphericalBesselJ` \u2014 so the general form implies both existing lemmas.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/SpecialFunctions/SphericalBessel/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "State the general form `HasDerivAt (deriv (sphericalBesselJ l)) (l * ((l-1) * x^(l-1-1)) * G l x + l * x^(l-1) * (-x * G (l+1) x) - ((l+1) * x^l * G (l+1) x + x^(l+1) * (-x * G (l+2) x))) x` for every `x` (the existing proof script with `x` for `0`), and derive `hasDerivAt_deriv_sphericalBesselJ_apply_zero` by `congr_deriv` + `norm_num` and the `x \u2260 0` ladder form via `sphericalBesselJDivPow_add_two`.",
